Fixed an External Integration's Remote URL and Headers being read raw rather than rendered, so a Jinja2 template in either reached the provider as a literal `{{ ... }}`.
Fixed `Default parameters` refusing `top_k`, `extra_body`, `reasoning_effort`, `n` and `logit_bias`, which Anthropic and self-hosted models legitimately use. A row already holding one could not be saved at all - including the edit that unticks `Enabled`.
Fixed a `timeout` of `null` or `0` in `Default parameters` defeating rule L6's default instead of falling through to it, and refused such a value at save time.
Fixed a persistently failing usage-record prune retrying on every model call, which put a whole-table delete on the consumer's hot path for as long as the fault lasted.
Fixed `usage_retention_days` being validated on the first prune of the day rather than at consumer startup, where every other configuration fault is reported.
Fixed the LLM Provider and LLM Model forms offering no `tags` field, and their bulk-edit forms offering no tag controls, though both filtersets filter on tags.
